<p>A hotel can have one video of the whole property, one video per room type, or both. Which one makes sense depends on where the video will be seen and what the viewer is trying to decide. This article walks through both options, what they cost and what happens when the rooms change.</p>

<h2>What is the difference?</h2>
<p>A <strong>property video</strong> shows the hotel as a whole: the setting, the entrance, the lobby, the restaurant, the terrace or pool, and a glimpse of a room or two. It answers the question "Do I want to stay here?"</p>
<p>A <strong>room type video</strong> shows one kind of room in detail: the bed, the seating area, the view, the bathroom, the small things. It answers the question "Which room should I book?"</p>
<p>Both are 60 to 90 second walkthroughs made from your existing photos, and both come in 16:9 and 9:16.</p>

<h2>When does one property video make sense?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Your home page.</strong> Visitors on the home page are still deciding whether your hotel fits. A property video gives them the overall feel.</li>
  <li><strong>Social media.</strong> On Instagram, TikTok or Facebook, people are not comparing rooms yet. The 9:16 version of a property video suits Reels and Stories.</li>
  <li><strong>Few or similar room types.</strong> If your rooms are much alike, one video that includes a typical room may be all you need.</li>
  <li><strong>A first step.</strong> One video is a low-cost way to see how video works for you before ordering more.</li>
</ul>

<h2>When do videos per room type make sense?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Booking pages.</strong> A guest choosing between a standard double, a superior room and a suite wants to see the differences. A video on each room page helps them compare.</li>
  <li><strong>Clearly different rooms.</strong> If one room type has a terrace, a sea view or a separate living area, a room video shows that better than a general tour.</li>
  <li><strong>Upselling.</strong> A video of a higher room category gives a guest something concrete to weigh up against the price difference.</li>
  <li><strong>Enquiries.</strong> When a guest asks about a specific room, you can send them that room's video.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Can you have both?</h2>
<p>Yes. For a hotel with several room types this is often the most useful setup: the property video on the home page and social media, and a room type video on each booking page. Each video is priced as one video.</p>

