<p>Two rounds of revisions are included with every video. You pay by bank transfer: in full before we start, or from €1,000, 50% when you order and 50% after delivery. See the full ladder on the <a href={pagePath(lang, 'pricing')}>pricing</a> page.</p>

<h2>Which photos do you need for each?</h2>
<p>For a <strong>property video</strong>: the outside of the hotel or its setting, the entrance, the main public spaces, any outdoor areas, and one or two rooms.</p>
<p>For a <strong>room type video</strong>: several photos of that room from different angles, the bathroom, the view if there is one, and a few details. A single photo per room type is usually too little for a 60 to 90 second film.</p>
<p>The video can only show what is in your photos. A bathroom, a balcony or a view that was never photographed will not be in the film, and we do not add guests, furniture or views. Sharp, well-lit, high-resolution photos give the best result; original files from your photographer work better than images saved from a booking site.</p>

<h2>Do you need to close a room for it?</h2>
<p>No. We work only from the photos you already have. Nobody needs to visit the property, and nothing has to be planned around guests. You send a link to your website or booking page, or the photos, and we do the rest. A person watches every video in full before delivery. We make up to 2 videos a day, and the delivery date is agreed with you beforehand.</p>

<h2>What happens after a renovation?</h2>
<p>When a room is renovated, refurnished or restyled, the video shows the old room. The fix is new photos and a new video. Send the new photos and we make a new video from them. That counts as a new video, not as a revision, because revisions are changes with the same photos and the same concept.</p>
<p>This is one reason room type videos are practical: if you renovate one room category, you only replace that one video, not your whole property film.</p>

<h2>So which should you choose?</h2>
<p>If you mainly want something for your home page and social media, start with one property video. If guests book specific rooms on your website and compare them, add a video per room type. If you are unsure, start with the property video and one room type, and add the rest once you have seen them on your own site. More on the <a href={pagePath(lang, 'hotel')}>hotel video</a> page.</p>

<h2>Try it with your own photos</h2>
<p>We make a free preview of 15 to 25 seconds, with a few shots from your own room or property photos, with no obligation and no invoice. <a href={pagePath(lang, 'contact')}>Send us a link to your website or booking page</a> and see your hotel in motion before you decide.</p>
